    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2505.01484v2-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Given a text, can we determine whether it was generated by a large language model (LLM) or by a human? A widely studied approach to this problem is watermarking. We propose an undetectable and elementary watermarking scheme in the closed setting. Also, in the harder open setting, where the adversary has access to most of the model, we propose an unremovable watermarking scheme.
        
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2505.01484v2-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Given a text, can we determine whether it was generated by a large language model (LLM) or by a human? A widely studied approach to this problem is watermarking. We propose an undetectable and elementary watermarking scheme in the closed setting. Also, in the harder open setting, where the adversary has access to most of the model, we propose an unremovable watermarking scheme.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2505.01484v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2505.01484v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
